# Circular Reasoning. A closed four-Observer loop: a 2x2 flat ring where each
# Observer's facing points into the next cell round the square, so every pulse
# retriggers the one behind it and the clock never stops. Both rotational senses
# are tested, which also makes the check correct whichever way round the vanilla
# `facing` state is read (observed face or output face) - one sense or the other
# always matches a real working ring.
# Origins sweep a 3x3 footprint at the player's feet level and one below, so the
# ring counts whether you are standing on top of it or right beside it.
# Dispatched through @r from bucket_slow: at most one player is scanned per cycle.
execute if block ~-2 ~-1 ~-2 minecraft:observer[facing=east] if block ~-1 ~-1 ~-2 minecraft:observer[facing=south] if block ~-1 ~-1 ~-1 minecraft:observer[facing=west] if block ~-2 ~-1 ~-1 minecraft:observer[facing=north] run advancement grant @s only bacaphd:redstone/circular_reasoning
